 # Ontology
 
 The system is opinionated: it names one default for each choice, and every default carries references to its sources and the alternatives it weighed (EE-014). Its nouns follow one rule: **standards first**. Use an established term with its standard meaning, and coin a word (marked "ours") only when none exists.
 
-- Canonical: `docs/ontology.json`. This page is generated from it; regenerate with `node schema/check-nouns.mjs --md`.
-- `node schema/check-nouns.mjs` fails when a retired noun reappears in the schema, design docs, Product Anatomy, AGENTS.md or README.md, when a noun has no standard, or when a function's capabilities are missing, retired or owned by another function.
+- Canonical: `docs/ontology.json`. This page is generated from it; regenerate with `node schema/check-nouns.mjs --md`. The graph is [docs/noun-graph.md](noun-graph.md), regenerated with `node schema/check-nouns.mjs --graph`.
+- `node schema/check-nouns.mjs` fails when a retired noun reappears in the schema, design docs, Product Anatomy, AGENTS.md or README.md, when a noun has no standard, or when a function's capabilities are missing, retired or owned by another function. It also fails when a relation's type is outside the closed set, when its target is missing or retired, when a noun relates to itself, when broader and narrower disagree, or when broader or part-of cycles.
 - Each noun names a `function` (one id from `operations/departments.json`, or nothing when the word is shared) and a handoff type (yes when that noun can type a package). A shared noun may appear in any package and never decides which function the package belongs to.
 - `node schema/check-nouns.mjs --package <file> --function <id>` prints one verdict: admit, refer to the function that owns the type, or reject. `--record` appends that verdict to `<id>.provenance.jsonl` beside the package. The verdict is not stored on the handoff. The receiver has to be a function noun. A schema checker that cannot run exits 2 and records nothing.
 - A scoped noun is written `name@function`. The suffix is a function id, and the noun's function is that same id. A bare name is not added beside a scoped sense. A retired bare name may stay, as the pointer to the senses that replaced it.
+- A function gets a new scoped sense (`name@function`) only when the meaning differs. The same meaning, presented differently by market or by relationship, is a view of the same noun, not a new sense.
+- A noun may carry relations to other nouns. The types are a closed set: `broader`, `narrower` and `related` (W3C SKOS), plus `part-of` and `derived-from`. `broader` and `narrower` are inverses, and `related` is symmetric. Stating one side is enough: the check derives the other, and when both sides are written they must agree. `part-of` and `derived-from` have no inverse in the set, so they are stored only in the direction written. A noun does not relate to itself. A target must be a noun that exists and is not retired. `broader` and `part-of` have no cycles.
 - A fact value is the boolean true or a record. Any other value fails that property. Two records that give one field two values are a reject. A record the term cannot read fails every property of that type. That is a reject of the package, and it is recorded.
 - References are ids in `<layer>/references/references.json`.
 - The genus of the whole is open: files say "the system" until the first venture runs end to end, then it is settled as an operating system or an operating model.
